cff-version: 1.2.0
title: subgmres
abstract: >-
  GMRES that minimizes the residual in an inner-product norm chosen
  independently of the preconditioner, and that monitors the norms of the
  residual's subvectors, each of which may be given its own convergence
  tolerance. Parallel implementations in MATLAB/Octave and in Python.
type: software
message: >-
  If you use this software in scientific work, please cite the accompanying
  paper.
authors:
  - family-names: Herzog
    given-names: Roland
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2164-6575
    email: roland.herzog@iwr.uni-heidelberg.de
    affiliation: >-
      Interdisciplinary Center for Scientific Computing, Heidelberg University,
      69120 Heidelberg, Germany
  - family-names: Soodhalter
    given-names: Kirk M.
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0612-1199
    email: ksoodha@maths.tcd.ie
    affiliation: Trinity College Dublin, The University of Dublin, Ireland
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/scoop-group/subgmres
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-05
keywords:
  - GMRES
  - Krylov subspace methods
  - preconditioning
  - saddle-point problems
  - residual subvector norms
# One field is still missing: doi, the Zenodo CONCEPT DOI, which resolves to the
# most recent version. It does not exist until Zenodo has archived the first
# release, so it is left out rather than guessed, and added afterwards.
# "unpublished" is accurate rather than provisional: the code is released before
# the manuscript is submitted. Once it is on arXiv this becomes a preprint entry
# carrying the arXiv DOI, and later an article entry if it is published.
preferred-citation:
  type: unpublished
  title: A Unified View of Residual Norm Minimizing Krylov Subspace Methods
  year: 2026
  authors:
    - family-names: Herzog
      given-names: Roland
      orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2164-6575
